Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T15:21:31-08:00","id":835419,"title":"","content":"Regardless of the oficial ones which ones do you want to see? And what do you want to see in the official ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T15:37:03-08:00","id":835428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=835290#post835290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess? This has been the case for years and I mention it virtually every time I talk about the TC core.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why would we put Aberrant in the TC core?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't saying Aberrant was TC Core, I just always saw Aberrant as the &quot;today&quot; game. I figured the first book was gonna be Trinity Continuum: Aeon, and hadn't realized there'd be a book just called &quot;Trinity Continuum.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also I haven't been following Trinity Continuum actively until recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T20:08:38-08:00","id":835545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=835428#post835428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't saying Aberrant was TC Core, I just always saw Aberrant as the &quot;today&quot; game. I figured the first book was gonna be Trinity Continuum: Aeon, and hadn't realized there'd be a book just called &quot;Trinity Continuum.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also I haven't been following Trinity Continuum actively until recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned upthread, Aberrant was the &quot;near future&quot; line. It was released in 1999, and depicted the world of 2008, nearly a decade in the future.<br /> <br /> Rather than do 2008 again, which at this point is eight years in the past, we're pushing it forward so it's once again the near future, and gives us room for a present-day setting. 2028 also works out better for a number of other reasons I haven't yet disclosed.<br /> <br /> From the <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/1u6sW4G.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">page spread</a> found in the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/133632?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=OPPforum\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path 2014-2015 Brochure</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brochure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Every Age Has Its Heroes.</b><br /> <br /> At long last, the Trinity Continuum returns in this new edition with a new system and setting revised from the ground up. Talents: the subtle champions, daredevils of unparalleled skill and luck. Psiads: those able to employ the powers of their own minds to affect those around them. Novas: the stalwart few with the power to alter the very fabric of reality. These Inspired arise in times of need. Few of them will ever sit idly: they seem to be driven to act. Some will be crowned as heroes, others as power-mad aberrations. Which will you be?<br /> <br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum Rulebook</b><br /> <br /> Our modern world is fraught with dangers, from the products of mad science and corporate greed to the perils of lost civilizations. Fortunately, as many of the Talented will tell you, danger is their middle name, and the \u00c6on Society is here to help them put things to right. The only constant in the world is change, and that's where you come in.<br /> <br /> The <b>Trinity Continuum Rulebook</b> will include:<br /> <br /> * A comprehensive guide to the brand new rule system all Continuum games share<br /> * A modern-day action-adventure setting which acts as an introduction to the greater Trinity Continuum<br /> * A full guide to playing Talents, their Gifts, and the various allegiances to which they may belong.<br /> <br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b><br /> <br /> In a world still recovering from a devastating war with horrifying mutated Aberrants, the last thing humanity wants to hear is that they're back, and they want Earth. Fortunately, Orders have arisen, each responsible for the creation of a specialized type of psion ready to combat the Aberrant menace. Will it be enough? A battle rages among the stars, and the psions are humanity's best weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> will include:<br /> <br /> * A full 22nd century setting featuring Earth's first steps into the greater galaxy<br /> * A guide to psions, the powerful artificially-created psi-users produced by the quixotic Psi Orders.<br /> * A GM-only section detailing some of the setting's secrets and potential future fates.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T21:02:08-08:00","id":835566,"title":"","content":"Dunno if its part of the plan but...<br /> World War II.<br /> The mysticism, the pulp/super heroes. Characters who serve their countries as symbols of justice etc.. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T02:05:30-08:00","id":836304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=835566#post835566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno if its part of the plan but...<br /> World War II.<br /> The mysticism, the pulp/super heroes. Characters who serve their countries as symbols of justice etc..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm just going to pitch the idea again that Max and Michael's 1945 showdown can literally happen at TRINITY (Almogordo New Mexico) on July 16th, at 5 in the morning. There's a reason they were both assumed dead when no remains were found...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Michael was trying to use the explosion to cause planetary eruptions, Maxwell obviously trying to stop him as the fallout would cost the lives of the bulk of the remaining non-Nova population, and human development shouldn't be forced. The blast is what threw Maxwell to the 22nd Century </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T22:39:41-08:00","id":836866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=835545#post835545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As mentioned upthread, Aberrant was the &quot;near future&quot; line. It was released in 1999, and depicted the world of 2008, nearly a decade in the future.<br /> <br /> Rather than do 2008 again, which at this point is eight years in the past, we're pushing it forward so it's once again the near future, and gives us room for a present-day setting. 2028 also works out better for a number of other reasons I haven't yet disclosed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question this raises for me though is when is N-Day. In the original game, N-Day timed roughly with the line's launch, with the setting being the not to distant future once the initial chaos gave way to the established Nova Age. Obviously N-Day won't be &quot;present day&quot; this edition, as &quot;present day&quot; is the Trinity Continuum core.<br /> <br /> Unless of course, as Aberrant won't be out for a few years, N-Day is timed with the release of the Aberrant setting, a few years after the release of the Continuum Core...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T00:22:52-08:00","id":836894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=836866#post836866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question this raises for me though is when is N-Day. In the original game, N-Day timed roughly with the line's launch, with the setting being the not to distant future once the initial chaos gave way to the established Nova Age. Obviously N-Day won't be &quot;present day&quot; this edition, as &quot;present day&quot; is the Trinity Continuum core.<br /> <br /> Unless of course, as Aberrant won't be out for a few years, N-Day is timed with the release of the Aberrant setting, a few years after the release of the Continuum Core...</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything in Aberrant's pushed forward about 20 years from the original setting, putting N-Day about 2018.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T01:12:23-08:00","id":836914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=836894#post836894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything in Aberrant's pushed forward about 20 years from the original setting, putting N-Day about 2018.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which could plausibly time with Aberrant's release *crosses fingers*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T06:27:10-08:00","id":837507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=836914#post836914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which could plausibly time with Aberrant's release *crosses fingers*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Boo. I would think it would be out before then. I have the utmost faith in Ian &amp; Company","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T08:44:26-08:00","id":837585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=834812#post834812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between Adventure! and Trinity Continuum <b>(the modern era could use it's own name, really...)</b> I believe we will have WWII as a setting. There are a few other options, but that seems most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've recently taken to calling it \u201cAction\u201d, given its action movie parallels. <br /> <br /> Before Adventure, I'm hoping for a Steampunk/Wild West setting, and maybe a swashbuckler setting; between Adventure and Action, I'm hoping for WWII; after Aeon, I'd like to see full-on space opera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:07:31-08:00","id":837643,"title":"","content":"I would love a WWII setting, but I would prefer to have it as some sort of mini supplement, and instead we could get a full supplement focused on the cold war, talents are prefect for james bond and spy like games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:49:06-08:00","id":837781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=837507#post837507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Boo. I would think it would be out before then. I have the utmost faith in Ian &amp; Company</div> </div> </div> </div>Well with the core this year, and presumably Aeon early next year, I suppose a 2017 release is possible. It'd be a tight push though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T19:58:36-08:00","id":837883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=837781#post837781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well with the core this year, and presumably Aeon early next year, I suppose a 2017 release is possible. It'd be a tight push though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan has always been to release the TC core and Aeon at the same time if at all possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T20:55:16-08:00","id":837907,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite comic story arcs was JLA's Obsidian Age, taking place in apparently 1000 BC, though I imagine a lot of liberty was taken with what existed, even overlooking Atlantis and technically it was the Iron Age. It depicted a more savage era of 'heroes.'<br /> <br /> So that general time period.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel_dc/images/6/6f/League_of_Ancients_001.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:04:23-08:00","id":838158,"title":"","content":"I strongly second Space Opera. A Time War campaign setting up several Eras could be fun too. The Twenties, the Near Future, and the early Interstellar period (i.e. the three from before) were also wonderful. With a Time War campaign you could do some alternate histories as well. Novas creating their own Atlantis in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cenozoic#Quaternary\" target=\"_blank\">Pliocene</a> maybe in a dry Mediterranean Sea bed. A Steampunk Victorian age. An Elizabethan England with Martian colonies, or a post-Atomic wasteland 1980's. Given Punk Fashions it would be hard to notice at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-27-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T04:55:57-08:00","id":839068,"title":"","content":"The name Continuum holds the key for reconciling all of this. When I finished my epic Adventure/Aberrant/Trinity game 10+ years ago, I thought the story was over. There was a small-scale sequel story that used a custom system to play more space opera but that fizzled and the universe went to sleep.<br /> <br /> Then I heard Onyx Path bought the rights and we're updating the games. Once the term Continuum was used, it sparked an idea to fold in the old with the inevitable return of Trinity.<br /> <br /> &quot;There are infinite universes, parallel to one another in an endless multiverse. Every possible event has occurred or will occur...or so we thought. Oddly, The Hammersmith Incident happened in only a handful of universes. The story of one of them is well documented.<br /> This is the story of the rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> Revisit the Continuum in 2016.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11337-bastion","name":"Bastion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T05:18:12-08:00","id":839073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=839068#post839068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name Continuum holds the key for reconciling all of this. When I finished my epic Adventure/Aberrant/Trinity game 10+ years ago, I thought the story was over. There was a small-scale sequel story that used a custom system to play more space opera but that fizzled and the universe went to sleep.<br /> <br /> Then I heard Onyx Path bought the rights and we're updating the games. Once the term Continuum was used, it sparked an idea to fold in the old with the inevitable return of Trinity.<br /> <br /> &quot;There are infinite universes, parallel to one another in an endless multiverse. Every possible event has occurred or will occur...or so we thought. Oddly, The Hammersmith Incident happened in only a handful of universes. The story of one of them is well documented.<br /> This is the story of the rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> Revisit the Continuum in 2016.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuum dev Ian Watson <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/diving-into-the-continuum-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">is right behind this approach</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Trinity Continuum isn\u2019t a few dots in a straight line, it\u2019s a vast multiverse of wibbly-wobbly quantum probabilities. Anything <i>can</i> happen, so it\u2019s up to you and your cast to make it happen. This doesn\u2019t even broach the topic of nova powers or super-science technologies that let you dive into alternate worlds intentionally as part of your game. You can easily run an entire series on the core concept the Continuum is based on. We\u2019re giving you the keys to the rocket. Where do you want to take it? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T05:42:10-08:00","id":839085,"title":"","content":"What i whould like to see would be an ancient Timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:01:49-08:00","id":839342,"title":"","content":"I'd personally be very interested to see how the Anima setting and anything during the time between Hammersmith to N-Day appeal to me as potential eras of play. I'm really rather interested to see what the continuum looks like during down periods between Novas &amp; Psions when Talents are the biggest menaces/heroes - so the modern setting intrigues me as well. If we are talking purely theoretically, a future setting without FTL would be something i would look forward to - using relativity instead of inspired time travel (or whatever other goodies OP is cooking up for us) to experience the Continuum aspect of the settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T08:33:59-08:00","id":839928,"title":"","content":"Would love to see a Time Cops book dealing with seeing the various sectors of the continuum acting as dimensional raiders in a covert / low key war against each other with the PC's acting as a peacekeeping force. Sometimes forced to keep the boundaries in place even if that means bad things happen to good people just because they are on the wrong side of a dimensional barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:55:44-08:00","id":840117,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that's not really an era. But it <i>is</i> something I'd like to see, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:05:41-08:00","id":840431,"title":"","content":"Just an offhand flip-side to my parallel timeline pitched earlier, where the 2120s looks like people in the 1920s imagined, with pulpy Planetary Romance trappings and Adventure! character mechanics and themes....<br /> <br /> A timeline where the War of the Worlds straight up happens in the late Victorian age just like Wells described, and the remaining alien tech results in Psions emerging in the early 20th Century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:36:48-08:00","id":840470,"title":"","content":"If you get the chance, find a graphic novel called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_Traces\" target=\"_blank\">Scarlet Traces</a>. It's set in 1908, ten years following the events of the War of the Worlds. London is still in the process of <a href=\"http://www.forbiddenplanet.co.uk/blog/wp2013/wp-content/uploads/scarlet2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">being rebuilt</a>, but with technology adapted from the aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:40:01-08:00","id":840679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perverseness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=839928#post839928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would love to see a Time Cops book dealing with seeing the various sectors of the continuum acting as dimensional raiders in a covert / low key war against each other with the PC's acting as a peacekeeping force. Sometimes forced to keep the boundaries in place even if that means bad things happen to good people just because they are on the wrong side of a dimensional barrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually wouldn't surprise me at all hq for a time-travel campaign setting was the nature of the post-Aeon canon era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:40:33-08:00","id":840680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=840470#post840470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you get the chance, find a graphic novel called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_Traces\" target=\"_blank\">Scarlet Traces</a>. It's set in 1908, ten years following the events of the War of the Worlds. London is still in the process of <a href=\"http://www.forbiddenplanet.co.uk/blog/wp2013/wp-content/uploads/scarlet2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">being rebuilt</a>, but with technology adapted from the aliens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added to my Amazon wish list! Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:37:47-08:00","id":841027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=839085#post839085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i whould like to see would be an ancient Timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dub my Bronze Age Novas setting &quot;Aegis&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:51:30-08:00","id":841100,"title":"","content":"Ah\u2026 the Agents of Aegis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T12:06:42-08:00","id":841419,"title":"","content":"Besides the official timelines I'm interested in settings in the far future. Aeon-style there was the fan-made Millenium's Edge 2997 project (<a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/additional_content/aeonsociety/2997/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.rpgpost.com/additional_co...nsociety/2997/</a>). Also, the Orion's Arm project comes to mind (<a href=\"http://www.orionsarm.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.orionsarm.com/</a>), though this one would have to be heavily tweaked to suit the Trinity Continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T15:10:42-08:00","id":844170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=834666#post834666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, currently public:<ul><li>?</li> <li>?</li> <li>1924: Adventure!</li> <li>?</li> <li>Now: Trinity Continuum</li> <li>2028: Aberrant</li> <li>2084: Anima</li> <li>2123: Aeon</li> <li>?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Great list! I love Zenith/post-Zenith (don't get chubbies, Exalted fans) empires a la Dune or this comic called Low (about a post-post-post catastrophe Earth in the far flung future in which we've been forced to move into deep sea habitats. Their technology is giving out and a savior class of nobility called helmsmen has gone extinct. The inciting incident in the first issue is a deep space probe has returned possibly with the location of a habitable planet.) At any rate, the exciting thing about a number of these kinds of decline-and-fall settings is how relatable it can be. It's not necessarily decadence that does in the home colonies, it's apathy or even a cosmopolitan weltschmerz. While you can set stories in the empire's far-off conquests, it's just as interesting to see a fortress world centric stagnant bureaucracy at work. In general, I'm amped about all of these iterations. I'm not quite as schooled on the new system as I might like but I found the old system to be fairly mutable even if Aberrant was wildly over-powered in comparison to their other post-human cousins.<br /> <br /> Carry on with the dynamite work, all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","user":"Queen Anne Country","date":". 03-08-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T09:57:35-07:00","id":865989,"title":"","content":"Listen carefully, nerds. Rich spoiled another one of my planned settings during this podcast: <a href=\"http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/episode-0021-pug-life-eddy-webb-rich-thomas/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/epis...b-rich-thomas/</a><br /> <br /> Spoiler: you guys correctly guessed the name in this very thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T10:57:26-07:00","id":866015,"title":"","content":"ANeall: The Era of Neall","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T15:24:04-07:00","id":866146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=865989#post865989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listen carefully, nerds. Rich spoiled another one of my planned settings during this podcast: <a href=\"http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/episode-0021-pug-life-eddy-webb-rich-thomas/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/epis...b-rich-thomas/</a><br /> <br /> Spoiler: you guys correctly guessed the name in this very thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starts at 1 hour in (to save people time). Aegis, greek setting. Also &quot;maybe 'Atomic' for the 50s, or something like that&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T19:23:29-07:00","id":866218,"title":"","content":"<b>\u00c6gis </b>indeed! See also: Primoris' April 24, 1924 journal entry on p. 27 of Adventure!, and to a lesser extent, the December 4, 2003 Weekly World News clipping from p. 46 of the Aberrant Players Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Atomic</b> is just an off-the-cuff suggestion Rich made, which I may add to my plans if I come up with a good concept for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T21:59:42-07:00","id":866257,"title":"","content":"I actually think Atomic would be a great era, but then I'm a huge fan of the giant insect movies, using 'Them' as an example. This is the beginning of the end of America's Innocence (not as relevant for other nations), and the end of Colonialism is finally happening but not with out conflict. <br /> And while giant insects, mad scientist, and alien invasion are all &quot;camp&quot; stereotypes several are also pulp standards. This is the decade that birthed Rock n Roll, and the Space Race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T02:32:48-07:00","id":866327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=865989#post865989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listen carefully, nerds. Rich spoiled another one of my planned settings during this podcast: <a href=\"http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/episode-0021-pug-life-eddy-webb-rich-thomas/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rickacarroll.com/podcast/epis...b-rich-thomas/</a><br /> <br /> Spoiler: you guys correctly guessed the name in this very thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I clearly missed it on my listen through. Can anyone point out when it was said, or just clue me in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T05:06:21-07:00","id":866346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=866327#post866327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, I clearly missed it on my listen through. Can anyone point out when it was said, or just clue me in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> CHILL covers this above, and I confirm his statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T05:33:53-07:00","id":866351,"title":"","content":"I kind of figured we'd see the Greek myths. Good pick.<br /> <br /> I'll also put in a vote for <b>Atomic</b>.<br /> <br /> With the eras before the 21st century, just think what a nice <b>Planetary</b>-style game you could run!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:31:32-07:00","id":866380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=866218#post866218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u00c6gis </b>indeed! See also: Primoris' April 24, 1924 journal entry on p. 27 of Adventure!, and to a lesser extent, the December 4, 2003 Weekly World News clipping from p. 46 of the Aberrant Players Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>CALLED IT!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:39:23-07:00","id":866440,"title":"","content":"Is Atmoic age only the 50's? Or is it going to extend all over the cold war? A supplement in the cold war with james bond like adventures with talents would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 04-16-2016, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:17:25-07:00","id":866521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=866440#post866440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Atmoic age only the 50's? Or is it going to extend all over the cold war? A supplement in the cold war with james bond like adventures with talents would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Atomic isn't anything right now. Rich made an off-the-cuff suggestion. I may make use of it at a later date, but it's not currently on my list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:21:59-07:00","id":866559,"title":"","content":"I could see a Quantum \u201cboomlet\u201d in the mid-50s, a side effect of Dr. Primorius' defeat at the end of WWII and a preview of sorts of the later Aberrant era. To the extent that they draw inspiration from superhero comics, the heroes of this era would draw their inspiration from the likes of X-Men and Doom Patrol: they're outsiders with problematic powers in a society that hates and fears them \u2014 sometimes rightfully so. More generally, it goes with the 50s notion that atomic mutations are weird and dangerous. These \u201cAtomic Mutants\u201d exist at a stage between Adventure!'s Stalwarts (who, in Aberrant terms, are \u201cStealth Novas\u201d) and Aberrant's Novas, with their defining characteristic being that their Quantum Powers tend to be low-level and Taint-ridden. <br /> <br /> In the bigger picture, Primorius learns some valuable lessons here that he implements when he triggers the Aberrant era. Namely, the trigger for the Atomic era is effectively a \u201cdirty nuke\u201d that results in excessive Taint; this lets him build a \u201cclean nuke\u201d to trigger the Aberrant era which, while not <i>eliminating</i> Taint, makes it something much more manageable. <br /> <br /> This is also the first era where alien incursions are a thing, with the Roswell incident and alien infiltrators who either replace or possess humans. I'm not up on my \u00c6on lore; but I don't think this would be any of those aliens \u2014 which would raise the question of what happened to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T00:09:42-07:00","id":866705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=866218#post866218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u00c6gis </b>indeed! See also: Primoris' April 24, 1924 journal entry on p. 27 of Adventure!, and to a lesser extent, the December 4, 2003 Weekly World News clipping from p. 46 of the Aberrant Players Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Atomic</b> is just an off-the-cuff suggestion Rich made, which I may add to my plans if I come up with a good concept for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... ... Like, in reference to Primoris' statement that Stalwarts are gods in the Grecian sense? Like, Aegis will be an ancient Greece setting?<br /> <br /> Because that'd be... really awesome, actually.<br /> <br /> (And if there's a section about Rome, too, that'd be even more awesome.)<br /> <br /> Y'know, assuming that I haven't misunderstood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T02:01:45-07:00","id":866726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=866559#post866559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a Quantum \u201cboomlet\u201d in the mid-50s, a side effect of Dr. Primorius' defeat at the end of WWII and a preview of sorts of the later Aberrant era. To the extent that they draw inspiration from superhero comics, the heroes of this era would draw their inspiration from the likes of X-Men and Doom Patrol: they're outsiders with problematic powers in a society that hates and fears them \u2014 sometimes rightfully so. More generally, it goes with the 50s notion that atomic mutations are weird and dangerous. These \u201cAtomic Mutants\u201d exist at a stage between Adventure!'s Stalwarts (who, in Aberrant terms, are \u201cStealth Novas\u201d) and Aberrant's Novas, with their defining characteristic being that their Quantum Powers tend to be low-level and Taint-ridden. <br /> <br /> In the bigger picture, Primorius learns some valuable lessons here that he implements when he triggers the Aberrant era. Namely, the trigger for the Atomic era is effectively a \u201cdirty nuke\u201d that results in excessive Taint; this lets him build a \u201cclean nuke\u201d to trigger the Aberrant era which, while not <i>eliminating</i> Taint, makes it something much more manageable. <br /> <br /> This is also the first era where alien incursions are a thing, with the Roswell incident and alien infiltrators who either replace or possess humans. I'm not up on my \u00c6on lore; but I don't think this would be any of those aliens \u2014 which would raise the question of what happened to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said it before and I will say it again: Max and Michael's 1945 showdown,where they both disappeared, should really have been at Trinity, with Michael trying to use the first man made atomic explosion to trigger worldwide eruption. That blast is what hurls Maxwell into the 22nd Century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T04:35:03-07:00","id":866752,"title":"","content":"The 50s are perfect for a game.<br /> <br /> Just check this out for some inspiration: <a href=\"http://home.earthlink.net/~rkkman/frames/summaries/S8.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://home.earthlink.net/~rkkman/fr...mmaries/S8.htm</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T04:49:31-07:00","id":866753,"title":"","content":"The only thing is the Trinity timeline does in theory require the paranormal to stay at fringe knowledge until N-Day - which would substantially limit the ability to do the type of cheesy 50s scifi/horror like THEM!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:18:01-07:00","id":867185,"title":"","content":"<b>Adventure!</b> works under similar restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:44:37-07:00","id":867213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=867185#post867185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Adventure!</b> works under similar restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Adventure! draws on pulpy exploration and mystery-men adventures, that are a lot more plausibly not known by the general public than giant radioactive ants attacking a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T21:42:52-07:00","id":867365,"title":"","content":"Adventure! Has a fleet of blimps laying siege to NYC and no one remembers that. If I recall THEM the military took great effort to conceal the ants and the final battle took place underneath Los Angeles out of sight. So yes I can see reasonable attempts at this and have it work after all the AEON Society we currently know has worked with the government in the past to cover things up.<br /> This is still the era where Americans believe the government has the people's best interest in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T12:17:03-07:00","id":902211,"title":"","content":"Has Onyx Path confirmed that they are remaking Adventure!? I see it listed on the Trinity Page, but there isn't a link like there is for Aeon<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11622-cynn78","name":"cynn78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:33:38-07:00","id":902389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cynn78</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=902211#post902211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has Onyx Path confirmed that they are remaking Adventure!? I see it listed on the Trinity Page, but there isn't a link like there is for Aeon</div> </div> </div> </div>They have. Adventure isn't in development yet though, so there's nothing to link to. Same with Aberrant. And Aegis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:44:54-07:00","id":902423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cynn78</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=902211#post902211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has Onyx Path confirmed that they are remaking Adventure!? I see it listed on the Trinity Page, but there isn't a link like there is for Aeon</div> </div> </div> </div>I can feel your pain. I enjoyed all of them, but Adventure was my favourite from the three by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T09:55:42-07:00","id":902774,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear that it's confirmed. If they stick with the 20th anniversary stuff. I guess we may not see a remade Adventure! until 2021 which is very unfortunate as the rest of Trinity holds no interest for me or my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11622-cynn78","name":"cynn78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:01:37-07:00","id":902780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cynn78</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=902774#post902774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to hear that it's confirmed. If they stick with the 20th anniversary stuff. I guess we may not see a remade Adventure! until 2021 which is very unfortunate as the rest of Trinity holds no interest for me or my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not doing 20th anniversary stuff for Trinity. Adventure just isn't being worked on yet. I want Aberrant myself. Be patient. Also follow the Trinity Continuum book at least. If my guess is right, you'll need that one no matter what game you're playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:13:31-07:00","id":904242,"title":"","content":"I wish that Aberrant was the one being worked on personally, though Trinity and Adventure! are also pretty interesting and cool. I will of course by all three if not for completeness sake than because they are all pretty awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T22:07:46-07:00","id":905408,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they're working-on/releasing the first three in the original order: Aeon, Aberrant, Adventure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:36:29-07:00","id":908000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=905408#post905408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure they're working-on/releasing the first three in the original order: Aeon, Aberrant, Adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as anyone knows, this is the current plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:59:11-07:00","id":910904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=904242#post904242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish that Aberrant was the one being worked on personally, though Trinity and Adventure! are also pretty interesting and cool. I will of course by all three if not for completeness sake than because they are all pretty awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the same boat. Though I'm hella curious about the new alliterative new worlds too: Aegis, Anima, &quot;at&quot; cetera...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:14:58-07:00","id":910914,"title":"","content":"I'm even more interested in the possibility of exploring alternative timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T16:24:08-07:00","id":916477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=910904#post910904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm in the same boat. Though I'm hella curious about the new alliterative new worlds too: Aegis, Anima, &quot;at&quot; cetera...</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they changing Aberrant to something A-related but not Aberrant, (like your suggesstions of Aegis or Anima) or was that just other pocket ideas they presented.<br /> <br /> I always thought it weird that the main force in 'Aberrant' was called 'aberrant' rather than nova or something else as a title, since Aberrant is what they are when they go all wonky and really its about novas being novas and stuff at the time. But that is just my thoughts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=910914#post910914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm even more interested in the possibility of exploring alternative timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternate time lines are pretty cool. I think there is a lot of great potential to play out variants on what we have as the official history. And heck you could even combine it, a game where the players travel to alternate timelines and weorlds for adventure and resources and knoweldge is always potentially fun.<br /> <br /> (I do have to admit, I have always imagined that the story post core book is unwritten yet, even when its totally written. Like if your playing and Adventure! game the 21st century doesn't have to be what Aberrant or Trinity says; same with Aberrant as far as the 2100 war and Trinity stuff and taint an all that). I don't really like metaplot in the way they used to do it, though I do like potentials and possibilities and suggestions and ideas and such.<br /> <br /> But yeah alternate possibilities as camapign elements, totally sounds like an awesome idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T04:28:52-07:00","id":916771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=916477#post916477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are they changing Aberrant to something A-related but not Aberrant, (like your suggesstions of Aegis or Anima) or was that just other pocket ideas they presented.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Aegis and Anima are ideas that Ian has had to do supplements highlighting other time periods in the setting. They wouldn't necessarily be full game lines in of themselves, but would highlight other points along the timeline. Anima in particular would take place in the 2080's, between the Aberrant War and where Aeon picks up. Aegis would be, IIRC, an ancient Greek setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:42:01-07:00","id":916926,"title":"","content":"Space Opera, distant future and an alternate 20th century. The Alternate 20th century would show what off world Inspired and pre-event Novas were up to.<br /> <br /> Swashbucklers: 1550-1815, Daredevils and swords!<br /> <br /> Pre-Holocine: the inspired before the Ice Age ended! The secrets of Atlantis!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:37:33-07:00","id":916969,"title":"","content":"You know what I would love to see? An alternative world in which the Daredevils, Mesmerists, Stalwarts and their creations became public and had a real impact in their world. Jump into the present day and we are living in an atompunk world where history happened in a completely different way. It would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:13:04-07:00","id":917520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=916477#post916477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they changing Aberrant to something A-related but not Aberrant, (like your suggesstions of Aegis or Anima) or was that just other pocket ideas they presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>There has never been any internal discussion about changing Aberrant's name. Unless something drastic changes, it will continue to be Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:51:59-07:00","id":917589,"title":"","content":"I would like the idea of colonizing other worlds, like new Edens, or hell original Edens.<br /> <br /> Or breaching into Parallel worlds.<br /> <br /> Atlan/Atlantis style mythos of ancient cities that vanished?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:57:05-07:00","id":918232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=917589#post917589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like the idea of colonizing other worlds, like new Edens, or hell original Edens.<br /> <br /> Or breaching into Parallel worlds.<br /> <br /> Atlan/Atlantis style mythos of ancient cities that vanished?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I like this more than once, cause I really like this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:50:16-07:00","id":918788,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Eden world one could be Advent, as in return to Man's Homeworld. It maybe could even be about the End of Time where an ark is built to return to the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:35:01-08:00","id":1034348,"title":"","content":"I'm still holding out for the 1970s era that was teased at in the original sourcebook timelines. The age of the Shaft novels and movies, Stephen King's Carrie, The Six Million Dollar Man and The Bionic Woman, Jaws, The Stepford Wives, The Boys From Brazil, Enter the Dragon, Alice Cooper, The Omen, The Andromeda Strain, David Bowie's Ziggy Stardust and Thin White Duke periods, and the highly underrated work by Kurt Russell in the trilogy of The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes, Now You See Him Now You Don't and The Strongest Man in the World. There's a pretty endless gold mine of inspiration for weird ideas. <br /> <br /> The 1950s would also be pretty weird fun. The 50 foot woman, The Incredible Shrinking Man, The Creature from the Black Lagoon, The Devil Girl from Mars, Ro-Man the Moon Robot, and a rogue Body Snatcher must team up to battle Godzilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:52:57-08:00","id":1034515,"title":"","content":"What we really need is the Cold War with superpowers &amp; 60s/70s James Bond for real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:46:06-08:00","id":1036202,"title":"","content":"I thinking my idea of a <b>Time War</b> Supplement would need to be setting four. It would make all the other settings logical effects of the Time War, relatable to each other through the Time War, and easier to describe for Players and Storytellers.<br /> <br /> Every Idea discussed in this thread would fit in with the idea of the Time War.<br /> <br /> Just think how many of the background secrets could logically be minor details of the Time War. Heck even the aliens could be in on the struggle as well as different faction of <i>Time aware</i> humans. The Queen's Chrononauts anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-22-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:55:25-08:00","id":1041574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=834666#post834666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, currently public:<ul><li>?</li> <li>?</li> <li>1924: Adventure!</li> <li>?</li> <li>Now: Trinity Continuum</li> <li>2028: Aberrant</li> <li>2084: Anima</li> <li>2123: Aeon</li> <li>?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the first ? is in fact the Aegis, and we do get that 1970s setting; that leaves one before Adventure and that one after Aeon. The later is a better fit for &quot;Time Travel Shenanigans&quot;.<br /> <br /> With those limitations, what are you hoping for? That said I do expect there will be a number of supplements that aren't just settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:18:21-08:00","id":1041692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1041574#post1041574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming the first ? is in fact the Aegis, and we do get that 1970s setting; that leaves one before Adventure and that one after Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Aegis could cover a wider swath of ancient greece/pre-history. I think I may've referenced how interesting this French comic The Secret History is; could certainly be a strong influence on the continuum with an ur-trinity existing since the time the neanderthal was outbred or otherwise forgotten at a rest stop along humanity's evolution.<br /> You'd guess either the age of exploration or the age of enlightenment would make fairly rich settings for the pre-Adventure slot. I like the idea of &quot;time travel shenanigans&quot; being the final book. Sort of a way of catching it all in one net. I'm guessing the way RPGs and futurist sci-fi/sci-fantasy writing are going that there'd be some strong singularity angle. Personally, I think space opera is a little more fun than time-is-a-flat-circle transhumanism but it's not to say that we can't be totally wowed by the latter. <br /> <br /> Anyone else so ready for this game that they check this forum every other day? OK!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:38:54-08:00","id":1042478,"title":"","content":"Aegis (Greek mythology), unnamed Victorian setting (a la League of Extraordinary Gentlemen), Adventure!, Atomic (1950s monster movies), Aberrant, Anima (cyberpunk), Aeon, unnamed space opera setting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:45:57-08:00","id":1042532,"title":"","content":"Oh, I forgot one: Trinity Continuum core book (action movies)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T18:20:26-08:00","id":1048010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1042532#post1042532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I forgot one: Trinity Continuum core book (action movies)</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH I was not that amped about the modern, low-powered setting but I saw John Wick 2 this weekend and could not be more psyched to create those kinds of characters. Holy moly was that an entertaining movie. I think you could create a really cool world using &quot;Talents&quot; as Wick-like protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:34:28-08:00","id":1049498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=834666#post834666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, currently public:<ul><li>?</li> <li>?</li> <li>1924: Adventure!</li> <li>?</li> <li>Now: Trinity Continuum</li> <li>2028: Aberrant</li> <li>2084: Anima</li> <li>2123: Aeon</li> <li>?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>In between aegis and adventure, abomination. A victorian tales of monstrous science. Dr Jekyll, Frankenstein's monster. What happens when telluric energy is used for nefarious act of &quot;science&quot; .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:50:56-08:00","id":1057833,"title":"","content":"So the trinity core will be a modern version of Adventure. Seems like both the PSI and the Nova's have their own setting any chance of a far future setting staring the Daredevils? Seem like each setting explores one of the paths of human evolution first seen in Adventure and now core but the daredevil/talents setting has not been seen yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:38:25-08:00","id":1057939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1057833#post1057833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the trinity core will be a modern version of Adventure. Seems like both the PSI and the Nova's have their own setting any chance of a far future setting staring the Daredevils? Seem like each setting explores one of the paths of human evolution first seen in Adventure and now core but the daredevil/talents setting has not been seen yet</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trinity corebook <i>is</i> actually what you're asking for, as it focuses on the Talents - it doesn't deal with novas or psis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:13:16-08:00","id":1057946,"title":"","content":"The Trinity Continuum core contains information on playing Talents/daredevils.<br /> Trinity Continuum: Aeon contains information on playing psions.<br /> Trinity Continuum: Aberrant contains information on playing novas.<br /> Trinity Continuum: Adventure! contains information on playing low-powered versions of Talents, psions, and novas.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:58:06-08:00","id":1058164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1057946#post1057946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Trinity Continuum core contains information on playing Talents/daredevils.<br /> Trinity Continuum: Aeon contains information on playing psions.<br /> Trinity Continuum: Aberrant contains information on playing novas.<br /> Trinity Continuum: Adventure! contains information on playing low-powered versions of Talents, psions, and novas.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So...<br /> <br /> Core = Batman, Nightwing, Daredevil, Punisher?<br /> Aeon = Professor X, Jean Grey, Emma Frost?<br /> Aberrant = Colossus, Wolverine, Superman<br /> Adventure! = Generation X, X-Men First Class, etc.?<br /> <br /> Not to pigeon anything down so simply. Just wondering in terms of power levels.<br /> <br /> And since I'm getting really, REALLY interested in this, Ian, what books are being Kickstarted at first? Just the core, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:03:13-08:00","id":1058224,"title":"","content":"Scion Kickstarted the &quot;core&quot; (Scion: Origin) and Scion: Hero at the same time. Likewise we will be doing the core and Aeon at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:49:32-08:00","id":1058790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1058164#post1058164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> Core = Batman, Nightwing, Daredevil, Punisher?<br /> Aeon = Professor X, Jean Grey, Emma Frost?<br /> Aberrant = Colossus, Wolverine, Superman<br /> Adventure! = Generation X, X-Men First Class, etc.?<br /> <br /> Not to pigeon anything down so simply. Just wondering in terms of power levels.<br /> <br /> And since I'm getting really, REALLY interested in this, Ian, what books are being Kickstarted at first? Just the core, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't comment on this edition, but in the previous edition Xavier, Jean, and Emma would probably be better represented as Novas than Psions, who are on a comparatively lower power level and have &quot;artificial enhancement&quot; as a central thematic feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:44:22-08:00","id":1158853,"title":"","content":"So in the Trinity Continuum blurb on the OPP website it mentions two eras/settings of play that aren't one of the 3 original settings, Aegis - set in ancient grease, and Anima - 2084 memory tech sci-fi, it also mentions that there are more settings not mentioned.<br /> <br /> What Settings would people like to see?<br /> <br /> personally I'm interested in post Aeon sci-fi like real far future space opera, what do others think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T04:14:20-08:00","id":1158869,"title":"","content":"-&gt; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...leases-and-why</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T05:04:20-08:00","id":1158885,"title":"","content":"oops sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T22:56:43-08:00","id":1160433,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see a problem with a new thread restarting discussion this much later...<br /> <br /> Allez: 17/18th Century Swashbuckling paramorphs with a touch of Baron Munchausen<br /> <br /> Abnatural: Victorian Steampunk/Horror<br /> <br /> Atomic: 1950s mutants, ufos, experiments, etc set against Cold War intrigue<br /> <br /> Aeternal: based in the distant future with a time travel/protect the Continuum focus<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Alternate Timeline settings...<br /> <br /> - War of the Worlds invasion happened in the late Victorian setting, and the left over tech let humanity unlock Psions in the early 20th Century (playing Aeon in the Adventure! timeframe)<br /> <br /> -Space exploration reveals a Planetary Romance Solar System (playing Adventure! in the Aeon timeframe)<br /> <br /> - Aberrant War is even worse and what\u2019s left is full on Mad Max/Fallout<br /> <br /> - Max failed to stop Michael, and the latter used the Trinity nuclear test to set off the Nova Age in the 1940s, historically syncing relatively closely with the Golden and later Silver age of comic book heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-20-2017, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T02:37:53-08:00","id":1160459,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of Abnatural, but i would rather a star trek ish space opera setting than what i think you have as Aeturnal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T05:07:22-08:00","id":1160486,"title":"","content":"Maybe they could do something like Exalted's &quot;Shards of the Exalted Dream&quot; for Trinity. A couple of alternative settings and might-have-beens. Could be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T15:33:17-08:00","id":1161629,"title":"","content":"I repeat my long standing desire for a 1970s setting. If I can't have Steve Austin, Jamie Summers, Wonder Woman, Shaft, Carl Kolchak, and Bruce Lee team up to stop Richard Nixon and his evil army of Vampire Space Bigfoots, then the Terrorists will have won, damn it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T12:41:38-08:00","id":1173814,"title":"","content":"So I assume since the Trinity Continuum Core setting is the present, but N-Day is 2018, the teased multiple timelines feature of the Continuum will play into keeping the core setting viable without canon saying \u201cok now Novas are erupting all over the world\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-07-2018, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T13:36:12-08:00","id":1174124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1173814#post1173814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I assume since the Trinity Continuum Core setting is the present, but N-Day is 2018, the teased multiple timelines feature of the Continuum will play into keeping the core setting viable without canon saying \u201cok now Novas are erupting all over the world\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From RPGnet &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734129-GenCon-Trinity-Continuum-Tease\" target=\"_blank\">GenCon Trinity Continuum Tease</a>,&quot; post 135, August 22, 2014:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So what happens when &quot;now&quot; starts to intersect with &quot;N-Day&quot;?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As far as I'm concerned, nothing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If we're still doing modern-era books by then, they will continue without the assumption that N-Day is happening.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">These books are about options, not limitations. We're already tinkering with timelines and probabilities. Nothing quite hammers home &quot;this doesn't have to happen&quot; like </span></span><i>it not happening</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:04:41-08:00","id":1174153,"title":"","content":"I'm now bouncing around timelines to use at the table....<br /> <br /> Timeline Alpha: Aberrant-Anima-Aeon canon<br /> <br /> Timeline Beta: N-Day never happens and the Continuum Core setting keeps up with present day<br /> <br /> Timeline Gamma: the Aberrant War ends into total nuclear devastation leaving a Mad Max/Fallout setting<br /> <br /> Timeline Delta: Inspiration Age never ends, and Stalwarts, Mesmerists, and Daredevils continue into a Planetary Romance future<br /> <br /> Timeline Epsilon: Max fails to stop Mal from setting off N-Day in the 1940s, leading to a &quot;Silver Age&quot; style Nova age in the decades that follow; which also creates a Mal-victorious Aberrant godkings era in the 21st Century<br /> <br /> Timeline Zeta: Aliens invade in the late 19th Century (ala War of the Worlds), the left over tech from which lets humanity create Psions in the early 20th Century as they rebuild<br /> <br /> ....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T04:50:38-08:00","id":1174245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1174124#post1174124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> From RPGnet &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734129-GenCon-Trinity-Continuum-Tease\" target=\"_blank\">GenCon Trinity Continuum Tease</a>,&quot; post 135, August 22, 2014:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Will there be any support for people who <i>want</i> the crossover? Running TC: Core with Talents and secret conspiracies in a world where Novas are just starting to appear sounds like a fun short campaign. Would books covering that sort of thing fall under TC:Core, or TC:Aberrant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T05:40:04-08:00","id":1174250,"title":"","content":"I'm really excited about the possibility of alternative timelines. Maybe they can create a line of supplements called mirrors that deal with many what-if scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T11:12:39-08:00","id":1174318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1174245#post1174245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be any support for people who <i>want</i> the crossover? Running TC: Core with Talents and secret conspiracies in a world where Novas are just starting to appear sounds like a fun short campaign. Would books covering that sort of thing fall under TC:Core, or TC:Aberrant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you wont see anything nova related (mechanics-wise) until they get to the Aberrant book. It would make sense, keep each book mechanically and setting themed so you know which books to get for what. Better organized that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 01-09-2018, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:47:57-08:00","id":1174341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1174245#post1174245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be any support for people who <i>want</i> the crossover? Running TC: Core with Talents and secret conspiracies in a world where Novas are just starting to appear sounds like a fun short campaign. Would books covering that sort of thing fall under TC:Core, or TC:Aberrant?</div> </div> </div> </div>CHILL is correct: nova rules will come with Aberrant. And then there's nothing stopping you from using those nova rules in the modern era if you want.<br /> <br /> That's why we put Talents in the core, so you can use them with any of the subsequent eras if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T13:58:57-08:00","id":1174356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1174318#post1174318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing you wont see anything nova related (mechanics-wise) until they get to the Aberrant book. It would make sense, keep each booth mechanically and setting themed so you know which books to get for what. Better organized that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question was less mechanics, and more... structure and branding, I guess. And setting material, ideally. <br /> <br /> So at some point in the future, we'll have mechanics for Talents and Novas. Once those have been published, would a hypothetical &quot;Talents in a world of Aberrants&quot; source book be in the core line or in the Aberrant line? Because, as I understand it, neither line will assume that the other actually happened, because each era is essentially optional.<br /> <br /> But presumably, all of the shady conspiracies will have been thrown into disarray by Novas appearing. <i><b>If</b></i> you're wanting to assume both happen in your campaign, is there going to be support for using the transition period for a campaign? <br /> <br /> Obviously, it's most apparent between these two time periods as they're the closest chronologically (so far). But for me, the interconnectedness of the setting has always been one of it's strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T17:31:02-08:00","id":1174405,"title":"","content":"I certainly think an &quot;immediately N-Day&quot; supplement would be cool setting book. I'm pretty sure Talents are assumed playable in Aberrant without further coverage, given that the Continuum Core is the main rules engine book for all the eras.<br /> <br /> For example, while I'm sure &quot;Baseline-looking Enhanced Attribute Novas&quot; are still a thing in the Aberrant-Era, I'd put good money on the Directive being largely Talent-play focused this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-09-2018, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T17:34:42-08:00","id":1174406,"title":"","content":"My question, and I'll understand if it's something you can't answer yet, is what is your intended release schedule?<br /> <br /> Are you hoping to get multiple books out a year (Core, Aeon, Aberrant, Adventure all in 2018), or a book a year (Core/Aeon '18, Aberrant '19, Adventure '20 etc), or longer between books because, after all, you guys have a lot of lines going at the moment (All the WW stuff, Exalted, Pugmire, Mars, Scion, Trinity, am I missing something?).<br /> <br /> Also, are you likely to kickstart the books after Trinity core?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:12:57-08:00","id":1174595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1174153#post1174153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now bouncing around timelines to use at the table....<br /> <br /> Timeline Alpha: Aberrant-Anima-Aeon canon<br /> <br /> Timeline Beta: N-Day never happens and the Continuum Core setting keeps up with present day<br /> <br /> Timeline Gamma: the Aberrant War ends into total nuclear devastation leaving a Mad Max/Fallout setting<br /> <br /> Timeline Delta: Inspiration Age never ends, and Stalwarts, Mesmerists, and Daredevils continue into a Planetary Romance future<br /> <br /> Timeline Epsilon: Max fails to stop Mal from setting off N-Day in the 1940s, leading to a &amp;quot;Silver Age&amp;quot; style Nova age in the decades that follow; which also creates a Mal-victorious Aberrant godkings era in the 21st Century<br /> <br /> Timeline Zeta: Aliens invade in the late 19th Century (ala War of the Worlds), the left over tech from which lets humanity create Psions in the early 20th Century as they rebuild<br /> <br /> ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Omega Timeline: same through Anima, but Psions and Trinity fail against Colony and the returning Aberrants, and humanity is destroyed. Not really a playable setting like the above, just there as a thematic warning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T12:43:54-08:00","id":1176571,"title":"","content":"I once had the idea of a timeline where Adventure happens as normal, but the Aberrant age occurs from 1936 to 45 or about, and then the Trinity setting starts about 1956. I admit that this was mainly motivated by the idea of having one of the wealthiest and most influential men in 1962 America be a black man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T13:04:06-08:00","id":1176579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1174406#post1174406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question, and I'll understand if it's something you can't answer yet, is what is your intended release schedule?<br /> <br /> Are you hoping to get multiple books out a year (Core, Aeon, Aberrant, Adventure all in 2018), or a book a year (Core/Aeon '18, Aberrant '19, Adventure '20 etc), or longer between books because, after all, you guys have a lot of lines going at the moment (All the WW stuff, Exalted, Pugmire, Mars, Scion, Trinity, am I missing something?).<br /> <br /> Also, are you likely to kickstart the books after Trinity core?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not involved in development or anything so take this with a pinch of salt. I suspect the Onyx Path gang can't answer those questions right now - RichT has repeatedly said they don't give release schedules to avoid disappointing folks. I mean, IanW recently mentioned its been 5 years or so since he first pitched relaunching the Trinity Universe and I'm pretty sure from snippets online that he wanted to be much further along by now.... so not publicly listing a schedule seems to be a wise idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T17:54:24-08:00","id":1176638,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we generally don't do release dates for a number of reasons. Instead we have the production schedule seen weekly on the Monday Meeting Notes blog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1176579#post1176579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not involved in development or anything so take this with a pinch of salt. I suspect the Onyx Path gang can't answer those questions right now - RichT has repeatedly said they don't give release schedules to avoid disappointing folks. I mean, IanW recently mentioned its been 5 years or so since he first pitched relaunching the Trinity Universe and I'm pretty sure from snippets online that he wanted to be much further along by now.... so not publicly listing a schedule seems to be a wise idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hell, it's been longer than that. I first pitched it to Rich in... late 2005? Early 2006? Just before the sale of WW to CCP, anyway. It was, I think, around November 2011 as Rich was putting Onyx Path together that he asked me to re-send my pitch. So counting from then, it's been just over six years. But in terms of the start of active production, like writing up an outline and assembling writers, it's been closer to five years, yeah. Although come to think of it, probably still closer to six.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T05:47:22-08:00","id":1176757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1176638#post1176638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, hell, it's been longer than that. I first pitched it to Rich in... late 2005? Early 2006? Just before the sale of WW to CCP, anyway. It was, I think, around November 2011 as Rich was putting Onyx Path together that he asked me to re-send my pitch. So counting from then, it's been just over six years. But in terms of the start of active production, like writing up an outline and assembling writers, it's been closer to five years, yeah. Although come to think of it, probably still closer to six.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right....right.....I'd forgot you mentioned trying it that far back too. Damn, time flies man. Still, congrats on getting *this close* to rebooting the old thing, must feel awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T14:33:07-08:00","id":1182708,"title":"","content":"I think I see a missing item. Abnatural a ghosthunters psi setting in the 1960s and 1970s. Psi would be weak and mysterious, PC psi that is. In some ways this would be like the X-Files, except that it's the whole Aeon thing business in the background. The leftovers and detritus of other events are the cryptids and &quot;ghosts&quot; of this setting. The mood would be low key suspense. <br /> <br /> In setting many PCs would see these events as supernatural or alien. Agents of Aeon would make &quot;one&quot; type of Man in Black. But only one type among many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-05-2018, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T14:42:36-08:00","id":1182710,"title":"","content":"I'm still thinking a time war book, both as a setting in itself and a link between all other settings, would be a great addition to this line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T15:07:30-08:00","id":1182718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1182708#post1182708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I see a missing item. Abnatural a ghosthunters psi setting in the 1960s and 1970s. Psi would be weak and mysterious, PC psi that is. In some ways this would be like the X-Files, except that it's the whole Aeon thing business in the background. The leftovers and detritus of other events are the cryptids and &amp;quot;ghosts&amp;quot; of this setting. The mood would be low key suspense. <br /> <br /> In setting many PCs would see these events as supernatural or alien. Agents of Aeon would make &amp;quot;one&amp;quot; type of Man in Black. But only one type among many.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s kind of what I was thinking for a Victorian setting by that name, playing on the spiritualism/occultism of the era and gothic science fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T15:08:59-08:00","id":1182720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1182710#post1182710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still thinking a time war book, both as a setting in itself and a link between all other settings, would be a great addition to this line.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still what I\u2019m pondering the gameline based further in the future than Aeon might be. Time patrol based is a positive future trying to protect their timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T15:57:44-08:00","id":1182730,"title":"","content":"Post Aeon is Jack Kirby's Fourth World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T23:26:20-08:00","id":1182825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1182730#post1182730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post Aeon is Jack Kirby's Fourth World.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have an idea for an era in that style, but it's in a parallel timeline, not the future, where Mal succeeded and Novas rose as god-kings to eventually shepherd diverse planetary civilizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:58:41-08:00","id":1182861,"title":"","content":"A 70s~80s &quot;The Warriors&quot; style with gangs x gangs x vigilants/punishers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9243-oparra","name":"oparra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:14:38-08:00","id":1183039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1182718#post1182718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s kind of what I was thinking for a Victorian setting by that name, playing on the spiritualism/occultism of the era and gothic science fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both would work. Perhaps two settings detailed in one book with period sourcebooks for booth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:16:36-08:00","id":1183040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1182720#post1182720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is still what I\u2019m pondering the gameline based further in the future than Aeon might be. Time patrol based is a positive future trying to protect their timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see them as a good guy hero faction. Other factions would have lower goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T18:28:43-08:00","id":1183118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1182825#post1182825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have an idea for an era in that style, but it's in a parallel timeline, not the future, where Mal succeeded and Novas rose as god-kings to eventually shepherd diverse planetary civilizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that, a century or three after Aeon, there are entire planets of nigh-God like Novas out there, perhaps waging war against each other over philosophical differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T03:59:18-08:00","id":1185876,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I didn't think of it before, but an early Middle Ages Arthurian setting would be a great fit for the game. Using Adventure terminology, the Knights of the Round Table would be Daredevils, Witches and Wizards would be Mesmerists. I'm not sure though how Stalwarts would fit into it, maybe the Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:02:38-08:00","id":1185879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1185876#post1185876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe I didn't think of it before, but an early Middle Ages Arthurian setting would be a great fit for the game. Using Adventure terminology, the Knights of the Round Table would be Daredevils, Witches and Wizards would be Mesmerists. I'm not sure though how Stalwarts would fit into it, maybe the Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both mesmerists and stalwarts could be fay blooded or blessed. It's not the source of the powers it's how you interpret the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:03:38-08:00","id":1185880,"title":"","content":"By the way, the time war book could be named AGON. It means a contest or struggle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:29:16-08:00","id":1186672,"title":"","content":"I would like to see Trinity: Axis. I'm imagining a game set in WW2, with high powered heroes and villains operating beneath the cover of the massive warfare. Behind the scenes, countless splintered timelines spin off from critical moments, with a second war being fought by both contemporary characters and time travelers to decide which of the myriad possibilities will become the dominant timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T12:45:34-08:00","id":1186784,"title":"","content":"Set in the early 90's, Au Lait, where you play superpowered individuals working as baristas in Seattle during the height of the designer coffee boom. Divas Mal does show up, and you can tell he's the villain by the fact that he always orders stuff like a half soy/half coconut milk 3/4 caff latte with an extra shot no foam with one pump of raspberry and half a pump of maple, and the fact that he uses the words Grande and Venti even when he's not at a Starbucks.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T13:33:14-08:00","id":1186802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1185876#post1185876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe I didn't think of it before, but an early Middle Ages Arthurian setting would be a great fit for the game. Using Adventure terminology, the Knights of the Round Table would be Daredevils, Witches and Wizards would be Mesmerists. I'm not sure though how Stalwarts would fit into it, maybe the Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the Knights would be Stalwarts as well. <div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;My strength is as the strength of ten, because my heart is pure&quot;</i><br /> - Sir Galahad in Alfred, Lord Tennyson's Idylls of the King</div> <br /> The Green Knight is usually given magical transformation as his origin, but he's also so strongly associated with the Green Man legend in popular consciousness that &quot;supernatural being&quot; (Stalwart) seems completely reasonable. (If you've ever seen the old White Wolf/Sword &amp; Sorceries Studios Relics &amp; Rituals: Excalibur book for D20/OGL, there is a really cool bit of <a href=\"http://warriorsinart.blogspot.com/2015/11/the-green-knight-by-ron-spencer.html\" target=\"_blank\">art by Rob Spencer</a> for the Green Knight prestige class.) Jack Kirby's The Demon from DC Comics also offers an interesting possibility for a period Stalwart character. I'm not sure how one would do Tom McGowen's Sir MacHinery, though. <br /> <br /> I like this idea quite a bit. I nominate <b>Avalon</b> as a possible title. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T12:23:08-08:00","id":1188260,"title":"","content":"Post-Aeon space-fantasy space-opera, definitely! Good RPG's with plasma guns, space travels, thousands of alien species and such are surprisingly scarce, taking into account thepopularity of the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T03:22:50-08:00","id":1188821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1176571#post1176571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once had the idea of a timeline where Adventure happens as normal, but the Aberrant age occurs from 1936 to 45 or about, and then the Trinity setting starts about 1956. I admit that this was mainly motivated by the idea of having one of the wealthiest and most influential men in 1962 America be a black man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of moonbases in the 1960s. But the shattered post apocalyptic fascist USA has got to go. <br /> <br /> That was always a big problem for me with AEON. A world with no strong democracies and powerful organisations deticated to preventing any potential resurgence of democracy, how is hope viable? Unity in what purpose or goal? Sacrifice for what? Corperate profits and Chinese oligarchic supremacy don't strike me as the basis of a worthy world let alone a utopia.<br /> <br /> If we could retool the AEON setting and have China be a democracy that is overcoming China's deep and profound racism, a China with wisdom, integrety, and humility, then you'd have a world with some hope.<br /> <br /> As AEON stands the Psi orders equal, organised religion, coperate business, big crime, oligarchic bureaucracy, the military industrial complex, and Souless Science with a New Age loyal opposition. The Quantikinetics were obscurantist academic philosophy. None of these guys seem heroic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T06:16:43-08:00","id":1188850,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something or I'm bringing a Eurocentric point of view into things, but aren't Sudamaerica, Australia, the Bharati Commonwealth, Oceania, and the UAN democracies of one type or another?<br /> <br /> Also, I can somewhat see some of your comparisons about the Psi Orders (ISRA being the religion, Orgotek the business, The Legions as military industrial, and the Ministry as the bureaucrats), but who is big crime or soulless science? Nor\u00e7a and Upeo? I really didn't get this negative of a vibe about them when reading the previews...<br /> <br /> I mean, overall, while some of them do some questionable things and there are plenty of opportunities for conflict with the Orders, they seemed to be pretty optimistic/heroic/legitimately trying to make things better, at least for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T08:52:30-08:00","id":1188885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1188850#post1188850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something or I'm bringing a Eurocentric point of view into things, but aren't Sudamaerica, Australia, the Bharati Commonwealth, Oceania, and the UAN democracies of one type or another?<br /> <br /> Also, I can somewhat see some of your comparisons about the Psi Orders (ISRA being the religion, Orgotek the business, The Legions as military industrial, and the Ministry as the bureaucrats), but who is big crime or soulless science? Nor\u00e7a and Upeo? I really didn't get this negative of a vibe about them when reading the previews...<br /> <br /> I mean, overall, while some of them do some questionable things and there are plenty of opportunities for conflict with the Orders, they seemed to be pretty optimistic/heroic/legitimately trying to make things better, at least for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks to be very much a 1e-influenced picture, where Nor\u00e7a would be big crime, the Aesculapians would be soulless science, and most of the regions you mention either got significant coverage late in the line (Australia, Sudamerica) or not at all (the UAN and the Commonwealth), with Oceania-as-Oceania being new to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:01:05-08:00","id":1188887,"title":"","content":"Norca is clearly shown to be a cross between a Mafia and a nationalistic paramilitary group. The vitakinetics are shown as split between the Swiss organisation run by rigidly scientistic types with little use for real science or human feeling, and the Haitian group of fluffy new agers.<br /> <br /> I assume the Doyne picked the Proxies both to defend Earth and build limits into those defenses. Example: the Clairsentient Proxy can't remember whether he warns the other proxies about the alien invasion in the past or the future. Plus he's a bit to serene to care.<br /> <br /> They overdid the doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-23-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:38:46-08:00","id":1189076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1188887#post1188887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Norca is clearly shown to be a cross between a Mafia and a nationalistic paramilitary group. The vitakinetics are shown as split between the Swiss organisation run by rigidly scientistic types with little use for real science or human feeling, and the Haitian group of fluffy new agers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Break is not as bad in 2e on the Vks, Now both exist but they are seen as rival schools of thought rather than as a &quot;Civil war&quot; the Order in generally is functionally like the Red Cross/Doctors without borders but with psychic powers.<br /> <br /> Norca ISN'T either of those at all. They are a mix of experts in biotech and Green Activists who had no problem performing the occasional terrorist act. Now that they are terrorists is a thing. But they aren't connected to Cartels or Criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:20:02-08:00","id":1189175,"title":"","content":"If Norca is so noble explain the story sections of the gamebooks which includes details like Norca tolerating even delighting in rape and the brutal machismo of Norca culture. Greens on the whole don't think rape, either by brute force or low cunning, admirable or even tolerable. And there statements in the books by Norca members that they sell illegal drugs to North America both for profit and to hurt Americans including those wanting to restore democracy.<br /> <br /> Norca is the Farc with superpowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:56:12-08:00","id":1189186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1189175#post1189175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Norca is so noble explain the story sections of the gamebooks which includes details like Norca tolerating even delighting in rape and the brutal machismo of Norca culture. Greens on the whole don't think rape, either by brute force or low cunning, admirable or even tolerable. And there statements in the books by Norca members that they sell illegal drugs to North America both for profit and to hurt Americans including those wanting to restore democracy.<br /> <br /> Norca is the Farc with superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> None of which was carried over into 2e at all. I mean it seems rather clear 2e learned heavily from the mistakes of 1e, like having a Cartel as a Psi order. Sadly the FSA seems far more likely NOW than when they were first written up, so I can see why they stayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T05:11:46-08:00","id":1189198,"title":"","content":"We wanted TC: Aeon to be recognizable and mostly familiar to fans of Trinity 1e, but it's not the same setting. Organizational structures and events which occurred in 1e don't necessarily carry into the new edition. The events surrounding the Esperanza crash and disappearance of the teleporters are quite different, for example. Several of the psi orders are dramatically different from their 1e incarnations. If they're going to be criticized, it should be based on what's written about them in the new book, not what might have been written about them 20 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T05:37:22-08:00","id":1189202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/834262-what-eras-you-want-to-see-the-most-after-the-official-releases-and-why?p=1189198#post1189198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We wanted TC: Aeon to be recognizable and mostly familiar to fans of Trinity 1e, but it's not the same setting. Organizational structures and events which occurred in 1e don't necessarily carry into the new edition. The events surrounding the Esperanza crash and disappearance of the teleporters are quite different, for example. Several of the psi orders are dramatically different from their 1e incarnations. If they're going to be criticized, it should be based on what's written about them in the new book, not what might have been written about them 20 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having the orders, especially Norca, massively retooled is good news. Although I'm backing the kickstarter, I haven't had a chance to read any updates. I've access to only the printed sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-24-2018, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T11:50:34-08:00","id":1190731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/615016-trinity-continuum-anima?p=632715#post632715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're not currently planning an \u201cAeon + 100 years\u201d setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, especially after seeing the spoilers in <b>TC: \u00c6on</b>, I <i>want</i> an \u201c\u00c6on + 100 years\u201d setting! Start it with a long-delayed Venezuela Event, largely isolating the post-Event timeline from the pre-Event timeline, then bring in a new surge of Novas, Psiads, and Talents. Allow Talents to come into their own \u2014 first as conscious probability manipulators, then as sliders, and finally as time travelers. Which is where the Venezuela Event's temporal barrier comes into play, shielding the past from an invasion by unrestricted time travelers. <br /> <br /> Bring back the invasive hardtech of Anima with noetics serving as a check on their identity-degrading dangers. This can be done by humanity; but I'd rather see it initially take the form of a new alien race that succumbed to their hardtech and are now effectively a hive-mind machine race. <br /> <br /> And of course, there's the final war against the Doyen \u2014 though I see that as merely being one possible conflict in the setting, and potentially resolved early on, rather than the central and defining conflict of the era.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u201cWe don't need you! Now get the hell out of our galaxy!\u201d \u2014 John Sheridan, <i>Babylon 5</i></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}